{"uid":"eval/samplers.py","name":"samplers.py","qualname":"eval/samplers.py","kind":"module","file":"eval/samplers.py","line":1,"end_line":102,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Registry of sampler constructors for the HumanEval harness.","description":"Replaces the hardcoded `if mode == \"standard\": ... elif mode == \"hrm\": ...`\nchain in `eval.harness.make_sampler` with a decorator-based registry that\nmirrors the pattern in `claude-code-main/src/tools.ts`.\n\nThe pattern:\n  - `@register_sampler(\"name\")` decorates a factory function that\n    takes a `settings_kwargs` dict (already filtered for sampler-specific\n    keys) and returns an object with a `run()` method (or just a sampler\n    object that `harness.evaluate_problem` knows how to drive).\n  - `build_sampler(\"name\", settings_kwargs)` is the public entry point.\n  - `list_samplers()` returns the registered names for `--help` output.\n\nAdding a new sampler is then a one-decorator change, not an edit to\nthe harness's control flow.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["eval/samplers.py::SAMPLER_REGISTRY","eval/samplers.py::register_sampler","eval/samplers.py::list_samplers","eval/samplers.py::build_sampler"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
